# Workspace metadata cutover & parity (P3-D)

Prove **package ↔ metadata parity** for Denali, enable **per-tenant Strangler Fig cutover** without big-bang migration, and close the metadata platform phase with an updated enterprise assessment.

**Doc SoT:** this file · **Nano spec:** `TEMP/p3/p3-d-migration-parity.md` (historical local scratch `p3-d-migration-parity.md`; not fresh-clone authority — see docs/audits/snapshots/2026-07-31/psr-2b-temp-authority-inventory.yaml) v1.3

**Status (2026-06-21):** doc complete · **implementation complete** (12/12 nanos) · parity CI green · prod pilot still staging-only

---

## Executive summary

| Layer | P3-D delivers |
|-------|----------------|
| **Shadow parity (CI)** | Export checksum + data-surface deepEqual + golden tour + render plan specs |
| **Pilot cutover** | `WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED` + per-tenant binding + optional allowlist |
| **Rollback** | Clear binding / shrink allowlist / flag off — **no** canonical tour rewrite |
| **Vertical proof** | Starter/climbing metadata tenant with `platform.*` composites (P3-B) |
| **Denali maintenance** | README banner — field layout SoT moves to DB definitions |
| **Phase exit** | Assessment ≥ 9/10 + all parity specs green |

---

## Goals

| Goal | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Export ↔ seed parity | Live `export:workspace-definition` checksum matches committed `denali-v1.json` |
| Runtime parity | `adaptMetadataPayloadToWorkspacePlugin` + DB row ≡ package plugin for data surfaces |
| Golden tour | `tour-publish-ready.json` validates on metadata path (flag + binding) |
| Render plan parity | `buildRenderPlan` field ids + `compositeId` identical package vs metadata |
| New vertical proof | Starter/climbing vertical authored in builder (P3-C) runs end-to-end |
| Cutover | Strangler Fig — tenant binding + env flag; rollback = clear binding |
| Denali maintenance | Package frozen for new EPICs; metadata is SoT for field layout |

## Non-goals (P3-D v1)

- Big-bang global cutover (`WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED=true` for all prod tenants in one PR)
- Canonical tour data migration when repointing definition version
- Metadata-only tenant without package overlay (adapter requires overlay today — document future path)
- Deprecating `@app-tour/workspace-denali` npm package (maintenance mode, not removal)
- Upcasters / breaking schema evolution inside same `definitionId`
- Urban workspace full parity (Denali + one starter vertical sufficient for v1 exit)
- Production traffic shadow-compare middleware (CI shadow only in v1)

