| **Feature-flag rollout** | [OneUptime Strangler guide](https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-01-24-strangler-fig-migration-pattern/view) — per-tenant / kill-switch | `WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED` + `WORKSPACE_METADATA_TENANT_ALLOWLIST` |
| **Branch by abstraction** | Jez Humble / Paul Hammant — stable interface, swap implementation | `WorkspacePlugin` interface unchanged; data from DB or package |
| **Shadow parity (internal)** | [`industry-alignment-2026.md`](../phase-6/appendices/industry-alignment-2026.md) REQ-P6-015 | Golden fixtures + DP/RP assertion IDs |
| **Immutable revisions** | [Form.io Form Revisions](https://form.io/features/form-revisions-form-json-schema/) | Parity compares versioned JSON snapshot, not live package mutation |
| **Tranche governance** | [Averroa Strangler Fig](https://averroa.com/insights/enterprise-software-workflow-automation-insights/custom-development-integration/strangler-fig-pattern-decompose-a-monolith-safely/) — rollback design + audit evidence | Runbook + platform audit `TENANT_DEFINITION_*` |

### Migration stages (frozen)

Aligned with Phase 6 research ([`phase-6-denali-workspace-research.md`](../research/phase-6-denali-workspace-research.md)) and LaunchDarkly migration stages:

```text
Stage 0 — Off:      package path only (default prod)
Stage 1 — Shadow:   metadata path runs in CI parity specs; prod still package
Stage 2 — Pilot:    flag on + binding on 1–2 smoke tenants (staging first)
Stage 3 — Live:     expand tenant bindings; monitor validation/render metrics
Stage 4 — Complete: Denali field layout SoT = DB definition; package = hooks/composites only
```

| Principle | Application |
|-----------|-------------|
| Expand before contract | Add metadata tables + loader (P3-A) before removing package data fields |
| Shadow before cutover | Parity specs must green **before** any prod tenant binding |
| Per-request routing | `resolveWorkspacePluginForTenantById` — no global switch without flag |
| Rollback without migration | Clear `workspaceDefinitionId` on tenant → instant package path |
| Backward-compatible schema | Additive definition evolution only; breaking → new `definitionId` |
| No routing without monitoring | Pilot requires validation error rate baseline (see § Observability) |

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  REQ[API request + tenantId] --> FLAG{WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED?}
  FLAG -->|false| PKG[resolveWorkspacePluginForType]
  FLAG -->|true| BIND{tenant.workspaceDefinitionId set?}
  BIND -->|no| PKG
  BIND -->|yes| ALLOW{allowlist pass?}
  ALLOW -->|no| PKG
  ALLOW -->|yes| DB[(workspace_definition_versions)]
  DB --> ADP[adaptMetadataPayloadToWorkspacePlugin]
  ADP --> WP[WorkspacePlugin]
  PKG --> WP
  WP --> ENG[PlatformWizardEngine validate / buildRenderPlan]
```

---

## Two-lever cutover model

| Lever | Scope | Default | Role |
|-------|-------|---------|------|
| `WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED` | Process / environment | `false` | Master gate — when false, loader **never** reads DB |
| `tenants.workspaceDefinitionId` + `workspaceDefinitionVersion` | Per tenant | `null` | Actual cutover — set via Super Admin tab (P3-C) |
| `WORKSPACE_METADATA_TENANT_ALLOWLIST` (P3-D-N-007) | Optional env | empty = all tenants when flag on | Staged pilot — comma-separated tenant UUIDs |

**Resolution order** (in `resolveWorkspacePluginForTenant`):

```text
1. packagePlugin = resolveWorkspacePluginForType(workspaceType)   // always load overlay source
2. if !isWorkspaceMetadataEnabled() → return packagePlugin
3. if !metadataBinding?.definitionId → return packagePlugin
4. if allowlist configured && tenantId ∉ allowlist → return packagePlugin   // N-007
5. row = getPublishedVersion(definitionId, version)
6. return adaptMetadataPayloadToWorkspacePlugin(row.payload, packagePlugin)
```

**Cutover recipe (staging pilot):**

1. Seed definitions: `pnpm --filter @apps/api run db:seed` (includes `seedWorkspaceDefinitionsFromDir`)
2. Set `WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED=true` on API pods (staging only)
3. Optionally set `WORKSPACE_METADATA_TENANT_ALLOWLIST=<smoke-tenant-uuid>`
4. Super Admin → club → Workspace tab → assign `denali-tour-ops` @ version 1
5. Run operator smoke: create tour, validate, publish-ready golden path
6. Rollback: PATCH clear binding **or** remove tenant from allowlist — no tour rewrite

**Production first PR:** parity specs + docs only — **no** prod flag flip.

