### Ingress routing (P3-A-N-011 — G2)

Production persist when `WORKSPACE_METADATA_ENABLED=true`:

```text
validateCanonicalBeforePersist
  → validateCanonicalBeforePersistAsync
  → resolveWorkspacePluginForTenantContext(tenantId, workspaceType)
```

`validateCanonicalBeforePersistSync` remains for worker threads and when the metadata flag is off — not used for live metadata cutover. P0 files below still call package resolve on **sync-only** paths; parity CI does not require rewriting sync for flag-off dev.

| Priority | File | Call site |
|----------|------|-----------|
| P0 (async live) | `tours/canonical-validation.ts` | routes to async when flag on |
| P0 (sync legacy) | `tours/canonical-validation-sync.ts` | `validateCanonicalBeforePersistSync` |
| P0 | `tours/build-clone-tour-body.ts` | tenant context resolve ✅ |
| P0 | `settings/wizard-template-catalog.ts` | template baseline rows |
| P1 | `tours/list-tours-operator.ts` | list projection |
| P1 | `tours/get-tour-operator.ts` | detail projection |
| P1 | `workspace-drafts/workspace-drafts.service.ts` | draft validation |
| NO v1 | `settings/settings-registry.ts` | package catalog only |
| NO v1 | `marketing/should-invalidate-marketing-catalog.ts` | public catalog hook |

Parity CI **does not require** sync ingress wiring — specs call loader/adapter directly. Live cutover **does** require flag on + tenant binding.

### Dev seed vs immutable publish (critical)

| Context | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| P3-C production publish | INSERT new version row only — never UPDATE `payload` |
| Dev `seed-workspace-definitions.ts` | upsert for local iteration — **not** the production contract |
| P3-D parity CI | Re-export live Denali plugin → compare checksum to committed JSON |

